     "totals": "average",
     "format_rules": "* scale green\n* format $,.0f",
     "width": 680,
     "height": 300
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "6 · Matrix with a true total"
   },
   {
    "id": "tt_matrix_note",
    "type": "flograph.util.note",
    "pos": [
     1620,
     3040
    ],
    "params": {
     "text": "**6 · A matrix total.** Average revenue by region × product, with *Total row ▸ average*. The total is the average of the **rows** behind each column, not of the four cells above it — a cell built from many sales counts for more than one built from few. The heatmap leaves the total row out.",
     "width": 520,
     "height": 160
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": null
   },
   {
    "id": "tt_down",
    "type": "flograph.viz.show_table",
    "pos": [
     1620,
     2460
    ],
    "params": {
     "width": 520,
     "height": 420
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": "What went downstream"
   },
   {
    "id": "tt_out_note",
    "type": "flograph.util.note",
    "pos": [
     2380,
     2460
    ],
    "params": {
     "text": "**5 · Totals in output.** Grouped by quarter with a subtotal under each, and *Totals in output* ticked — so the table that leaves it carries a *Q1 Total*, *Q2 Total* and *Total* row, the way a spreadsheet's Subtotal command writes them.\n\n**What went downstream** has no rules of its own: it shows those rows as plain data. Untick *Totals in output* and they vanish from it, while the card on the left looks exactly the same.",
     "width": 460,
     "height": 240
    },
    "code": null,
    "label": null
   }
